    "source": [
-    "## 3. Project delivery and status (Q3)\n",
+    "## 3. Do flood-control investments overlap with flood-prone areas? (flood alignment)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**What:** build `analytics_flood_alignment`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Business question:** where are flood-control investments located relative to mapped MGB flood susceptibility, and how much recorded investment and how many projects fall in each susceptibility level?\n",
     "\n",
-    "**What:** build `analytics_project_delivery_status`. It answers: which regions and categories have the highest share of ongoing, inactive, or long-running projects? One row per region, category, and `status_group`. Key `0` regions are left out.\n",
+    "**Grain:** one row per official PSGC region and flood point class. Every region has one row for each class, even with no project, so the map legend and the area figures stay complete. Key `0` is left out. The regions are the `REGION` rows of view 1.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The flood point class is the Gold flood result at the project's own map point:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "| Class | From Gold |\n",
+    "| --- | --- |\n",
+    "| `Low`, `Moderate`, `High`, `Very High` | `flood_match_status = 'MATCHED'`, the level from `dim_flood_susceptibility` |\n",
+    "| `AMBIGUOUS` | The point sits in polygons of more than one level. No level is picked ([D-45](../../docs/decisions.md)). |\n",
+    "| `OUTSIDE_MAPPED_ZONES` | `UNMATCHED` with a valid point. MGB has no polygon there. Not low risk. |\n",
+    "| `NO_USABLE_POINT` | `UNMATCHED` without a valid point. Classification is unavailable. |\n",
+    "| `INVALID_SOURCE` | Silver could not classify the source row. |\n",
     "\n",
     "**Why:**\n",
     "\n",
-    "- Long-running reuses Gold's `long_running_flag` ([D-32](../../docs/decisions.md)). It is true when more than 24 months pass from start to completion, or to the snapshot date without a completion date. The view does not set its own threshold.\n",
-    "- The flag is `NULL` for a project without a start date, and `zero_progress_flag` is `NULL` when progress is unresolved. So each rate divides by the projects where its flag is known, not by every project. The `_evaluated_count` columns show those denominators.\n",
-    "- `pct_of_region_sector_projects` answers \"which regions and categories have the most ongoing or inactive work?\". The statuses of one region and sector add up to 100. `pct_of_region_projects` shows how big each group is within its region.\n",
-    "- An unmapped sector or status stays `NULL` ([D-37](../../docs/decisions.md)). `infra_type_mapping_status` says why the sector is empty. `status_mapping_status` says why the status is empty: `NO_SOURCE_STATUS` when Gold has no status for the project (key `0`), or `NO_APPROVED_STATUS_RULE` when the source status, often a shifted value, has no approved mapping ([Gold model](../../docs/gold_model.md#unmapped-values-stay-visible)). The view never writes `Unknown` or `Unmapped` text.\n",
-    "- Every official region keeps a row, with the same `source_coverage_status` as Q1. A region with no mapped project has one row with `project_count` 0 and empty sector, status, and reason columns, so it never disappears.\n",
+    "- The spatial match ran once in Silver Table 15. Gold resolved it to a key. This view only joins and counts. It parses no geometry and runs no spatial join.\n",
+    "- Flood-control is the broad DPWH flag `is_dpwh_flood_related` ([D-39](../../docs/decisions.md)), which includes the whole budget of Multi-sector projects with a flood component. The strict single-sector figures and the official flood-list figures sit beside it, so the real amount can be bracketed.\n",
+    "- Every project in a row is flood-control, other, or uncategorized. The three counts add up to `project_count`, so no project is hidden.\n",
+    "- The area columns come from the newest Gold exposure run. They fill only the level rows. Levels can overlap, so add level areas within a region only when `exposure_area_status` is `ADDITIVE_WITHIN_TOLERANCE` ([Gold model](../../docs/gold_model.md#fact_region_flood_exposure)).\n",
+    "- A region with no mapped DPWH project, such as BARMM, keeps `NULL` project figures, because the source cannot say.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Interpretation rule:** overlap does not prove that a project protects an area, or that it protects a whole region. A point outside mapped MGB polygons is **not** low risk. Keep `AMBIGUOUS`, `OUTSIDE_MAPPED_ZONES`, `NO_USABLE_POINT`, and `INVALID_SOURCE` visible next to the level rows.\n",
     "\n",
-    "**Reading the result:** a long-running or zero-progress project is not proof of delay. DPWH gives no reliable target completion date, so the repo does not label any project delayed ([Data model](../../docs/data-model.md#business-question-coverage-planned)). A high zero-progress rate can also mean progress was never reported, not that work stalled.\n",
+    "**Why region and not province:** the MGB area of each flood level exists only per region in Gold. Province flood exposure is deferred until its one-time Silver intersection is proven safe and affordable (D-57). Province flood context is available per project in view 5, from the same Gold flood result.\n",
     "\n",
-    "**Expected result:** one row per region, category, and status group, plus one row for each region with no mapped project. Within each region, `pct_of_region_projects` adds up to 100. Within each region and sector, `pct_of_region_sector_projects` adds up to 100."
+    "**Expected result:** one row per region and class. The class rows of each mapped region add up to its region project count in view 1."
    ]
